				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>Davidson's program is a program for by implication it's a program for a total semantics of some natural language and I think that this is a silly program at this stage in things all we can hope to do sensibly is to pick away into pieces and see where a pattern starts to emerge and follow it up and the kind of thing that Hans Kant does This is not what Davidson does and as a result I don't think if Davidson achieves anything it's rather by accident But there's no nothing's gained by saying that so why?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
