				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>No question month or task was worth I don't know It could be anything There's some historical bits in my book Sometimes I give a talk and occasionally bits of it written up appear somewhere on Present Aims of Model Theory that's a title I rather offer I'm sorry Oh I know Of course I know yes it was I'd suppressed the memory of it It was the paper with donor in the JSL Maybe for history I'd better set down the awful things that happened there John Downing John Downing Yes I undertook to collect together a set of essays on different aspects of Tuske's work in Loggy for the JSR and there was a hope we were working on this together at the beginning because you were the I was president Yes The hope was that we could get something out in time for his birthday celebrations but I could never get any kind of response from Berkeley I did write to people but they always referred me to other people and I had left a rather strong impression which I remember mentioning to you in a letter that somehow they just didn't want to be involved with it at this point they didn't want to say that And indeed shortly after he died I forget which of us whether it was I or they made the first move but it seemed that the log jam had cleared and Wilfred was reviews editor of JSO?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
