				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>There's an amazing remark by Taski somewhere in the thirties I think it may be in his late thirties write up of that material that he considers he's now answered all questions of interest in his own as a historical judgment it's an all time loser that these versions of his work here have been fundamental for all sorts of things that obviously he never dreamt of I think he had a clear selfcontained idea of what he hoped to achieve and he'd achieve that Do you think that could you make a generalization about that and other things that he did that would That's a very interesting question but it's the sort of point where I would refer to the solo and other people who work directly with Task.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
