			</ANNOTATION>
		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a81" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts160" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts161">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>This was fairly late on in the getting these articles ready for the JSO and I was still missing two namely Fanderpries tends to produce but at the last moment was a donor who seemed to have been a bit wettled He'd written these letters but he didn't see anything that he could do.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
				</ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
			</ANNOTATION>
		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a82" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts162" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts163">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>So at that point in order to chivy things these people along a bit To what to chivy them along Chivy them along their transpression Oh I probably got it wrong but I thought that was No It's not English and it's not American I wrote an article with some blank spaces in it some to be filled by Donor and some to be filled by Funding Res I then circulated to all the people involved in order to produce maximum impact How did it get so noisier I was just saying how it got so noisier literally Ampro people like okay I'll move this a little closer to you So go on this had the desired effect on Donor in the TM as he filled in blank spaces really very vigorously and promptly very interesting stuff he dug out about the nineteen thirty eight oh nine write up of the Real Close Fields material.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
				</ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
			</ANNOTATION>
		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a83" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts164" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts165">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>It was just the rails then I think the Real Close Fields only appeared in the nineteen forty nine And it had the desired effect on Clamp and Breeze too at least a manuscript from him appear very soon afterwards So as intended it was a success but as not intended it was rather a disaster because Vaugh was very angry at what he claimed were multiple distortions and inappropriate style not Tarski style in other words Well I don't know and he fingered you as the Well, yes I accept responsibility for it I've written it in an inappropriate style is that what you're saying?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
				</ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
			</ANNOTATION>
		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a84" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts166" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts167">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>Well that's my phrase Yeah right that's what I want your phrase What he seemed most annoyed about was a suggestion that Tarsky in the nineteen thirty seminar in Warsaw wasn't greatly interested in the matter of decidability he was much more interested in surveying the complete extensions of a given theory and the decidability came to the fore in Tarsky's own words when Tarsky went to work with the Rand Corporation The Rand Corporation This is Tuskey the book that Tarsky wrote in forty eight I think footnotes in ' forty nine where he says in the preface that he's brought the cirability questions to the fore because of the situation in which he's now working.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
				</ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
			</ANNOTATION>
		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a85" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts168" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts169">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>Of course it's after Church's Thesis and I want to come back to that Church's Thesis wasn't there in nineteen thirty and decidability was a slightly vague idea But I had a very difficult conversation with Vaught that lasted about fifteen minutes He was obviously quite five oh he was obviously quite unaware of the possible costs of this That may have been that may be confusing that may have been earlier in the business but I rewrote the relevant sections and Wort was so angry at this point and felt that his points had not been met I got a letter signed by Wort and Henkin together saying that what I'd written was a disgrace because of the many factual errors and inappropriate wordings in it They insisted that I should send the article to six people that they named for these six people's comments which would set me right.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
				</ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
			</ANNOTATION>
		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a86" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts170" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts171">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>Now I don't remember who all of them were but they included McIntyre and Tasky sorry and Claney and Church and Gregory Moore Now this is Gwen and what year somewhere around eighty six.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
				</ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
			</ANNOTATION>
		</TIER>
	<TIER TIER_ID="SPEAKER_01" LINGUISTIC_TYPE_REF="default-lt">
		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a3" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts4" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts5">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>Excuse me, just one second.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
