		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a43" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts84" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts85">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>Favorite favorite LEWS one Chap Lewis you say at Princeton now?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
				</ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
			</ANNOTATION>
		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a46" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts90" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts91">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>Why did he say Dutch?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
				</ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
			</ANNOTATION>
		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a52" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts102" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts103">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>I find it thinking about axioms for the Parthole relation very plausible in and of itself but what he was going to the axioms that he came up with were just so implausible But he published a book on that So besides that first thing you wrote on Tarski have you written other stuff?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
